A couple more things I am curious about if anyone can answer.
I have a keyboard plugin by
@ATT_Turan
from last Advent (I think) that I also use and it works great. I took a look at it because I thought that would need to map all of the keys on the keyboard so you could type. I can see parts of what it is doing, but that plugin doesn't make it so the keyboard keys are accessible outside of something like Name Input Processing. I was just wondering why that might be? Maybe that plugin was made to solely work in specific circumstances and it isn't mapping all those keys in general?
Also, is there any issue with mapping a bunch a keys with a new plugin solely for that? Like making this plugin map 30-40 keys? Many games use hotkeys to do things and I am thinking about experimenting with those mechanics.
Of course, the more keys you have mapped, I guess the larger the Parallel Event would need to be to check all the Conditional Branches to see if any are being triggered. Or maybe you would need to have multiple Parallel Events running to check them all without experiencing any sort of delay or performance impact?
Anyway, if there isn't any real issue with mapping a bunch of keys this way, I will make the plugin later today and do some testing.
Thanks again!

